SUMMARY:Annual Hackleberry Raspberry Night Hike!
DESCRIPTION:Metrotrails: NJ\, PA\, NY Metropolitan Area Hiking and More!\n
 Meetup in Chester at 4:00 PM\, shuttle a few cars to the start location to
  START HIKING at 4:30. Late meetups are difficult on this one due to the p
 oor cell service. Expect hilly\, mountainous terrain in the dark with two 
 good swim spots.\n\nROUTE TBA\, but generally this:\n\nJoin us on the 7th 
 Annual Raspberry Night hike\, where we will eat as many invasive Japanese 
 wine berries as we can find. We will take the old rail trail from Chester 
 for some nice shaded woods walking. We will then pop over into Hacklebarne
 y for some wine berries and a swim before some easy road walks and trails 
 to finish the night. Distance I'm shooting for is 10-12 miles.\n\nBring: W
 atershoes\, Hiking poles to cross river\, good footwear\, bug spray\, head
 lamp\, snacks\, water.\n\nI hope to see you there!!\n\n-Cupcake
